>> title: Country Fried Steak
>> category: Fried & Crispy
>> tags: beef, cube steak, southern, pan-fry, gravy
>> counters: Meat and Three, Diner, One Pot
>> aka: country-fried steak, chicken fried steak, chicken-fried steak, cubed steak, steak and gravy
>> servings: 4
>> time: 45 min
>> slack: narrow — they are fried one at a time; two in the pan drop the temperature and the crust turns to paste instead of browning
>> pairs-with: cream-gravy, macaroni-and-cheese, green-beans, creamed-corn
>> step.1: Fry them one at a time in half an inch of fat. The gravy afterwards is made from what browns in the pan.
>> step.2: pat dry
>> step.3: whisk the flour
>> step.4: beat the wash
>> step.5: flour, wash, flour again, rest 10 min
>> step.6: fry 6 min, turned once

Fry them one at a time in half an inch of fat. Two in the pan drops the temperature, the crust turns to paste, and the gravy afterwards has nothing browned in the pan to be made from.

Pat @beef cube steaks{4}(6 oz / 170 g each) dry.

Whisk @all-purpose flour{1 1/2%cup}(195 g), @fine sea salt{2%tsp}, @black pepper{2%tsp}, @garlic powder{1%tsp}, @paprika{1%tsp}.

Beat @large eggs{2}, @buttermilk{1/2%cup}(120 mL).

Dredge @&(~3)dried steaks{} through @&(~2)seasoned flour{}, @&(~1)egg wash{} and back into the flour, then ~rest{10%min} on a rack.

Fry @&(~1)breaded steaks{} in @vegetable oil{1%cup}(240 mL) at 350°F (175°C) in a #cast-iron skillet{} for ~fry{6%min}.

Ladle cream gravy over it at the pass. It is made in the same pan while the steaks sit.
